Subject: [PATCH] webrtc: relay UDP through SOCKS5, or create no UDP socket

WebRTC UDP sockets relay through the configured SOCKS5 proxy over a UDP
association, so host candidates carry the relay address and a remote
peer receives packets from the proxy's exit. With no proxy, WebRTC runs
direct. With a proxy that cannot carry datagrams, such as HTTP, HTTPS,
SOCKS4, a multi-hop chain, a PAC script or the system resolver, or a
SOCKS5 proxy that refuses UDP, WebRTC creates no UDP socket and the page
gets no UDP candidate. The browser logs each refusal with its reason.
Rewriting candidate text alone leaves packets arriving from the host's
real IP, which any peer can read.

